 {r}←SaveCrashRequest parms;c;d;e;h;m;b;cap;secret;get;keep
⍝ HandleError's `customFns` (see `SetErrorParms`): writes what the crashed thread was working on
⍝ next to the crash files, as `<crash>.request.json`, so that a crash caused by an ill-formed or
⍝ unexpected request can be investigated with that request at hand.
⍝ HandleError calls this in the thread that crashed, and Rumba serves every connection in a
⍝ thread of its own, so the thread number identifies the connection: see Rumba's
⍝ `GetConnectionOfThread`. Nothing is written for a thread that is not serving a connection.
⍝ The report holds the connection's last block of data exactly as received, and every message of
⍝ the connection: normally one, more when requests were pipelined. A message that was not fully
⍝ received may lack its request line and parsed headers; then the raw header is reported.
⍝ Values of headers that carry credentials are replaced by "***" (see `SecretHeaders`), and data
⍝ is capped, so the report holds neither live secrets nor the whole of a big upload.
⍝ Relies on `G` and `R` being around, just like `AppLog` does.
 r←⍬
 :If 0=⎕NC'G'
 :OrIf 9≠G.⎕NC'Server'
     :Return
 :EndIf
 c←G.Server R.GetConnectionOfThread ⎕TID
 :If ⍬≡c
     :Return
 :EndIf
 cap←65536                                          ⍝ Characters kept of `LastBlock` and of any content
 secret←SecretHeaders
 get←{0<⍺.⎕NC ⍵:⍺⍎⍵ ⋄ ''}                           ⍝ Properties may not exist yet
 keep←{(⍺⌊≢⍵)↑⍵}
 d←⎕NS''
 d.Time←A.FormatDateTime ⎕TS
 d.Thread←⎕TID
 d.PeerAddress←c get'PeerAddress'
 d.LastBlockLength←≢c get'LastBlock'
 d.LastBlock←secret MaskSecretHeaders cap keep c get'LastBlock'
 d.Messages←⍬
 :For m :In c get'Messages'
     e←⎕NS''
     e.StartLine←m get'StartLine'
     e.Method←m get'Method'
     e.RequestTarget←m get'RequestTarget'
     :If 0<m.⎕NC'Headers'
         h←m.Headers
         :If 0<≢h
             b←(1 ⎕C⊃¨h)∊secret
             h[⍸b]←{(⊃⍵)'***'}¨b/h
         :EndIf
         e.Headers←h
     :Else
         e.Header←secret MaskSecretHeaders m get'Header'  ⍝ Not parsed yet: the raw header
     :EndIf
     e.ContentLength←≢m get'Content'
     e.Content←cap keep m get'Content'
     e.(HeaderComplete ContentComplete)←m get¨'HeaderComplete' 'ContentComplete'
     d.Messages,←e
 :EndFor
 (⊂(⎕JSON⍠('Compact' 0))d)⎕NPUT(parms.crashFilename,'.request.json')1
⍝Done
